# Number formats: a column of numbers shown by a C `printf` conversion,
# without its `%`, after its type in brackets. The value is unchanged; only
# how it is shown. `'` would group the digits by the locale's separator,
# which this example leaves out so that it prints the same everywhere.

sheet Prices

Price  : Decimal[.2f]
Signed : Decimal[+.1f]
Sci    : Float[.3e]
Short  : Float[g]
Count  : Integer[05d]
Hex    : Integer[#x]
Bits   : Integer[08b]

| Item   | Price     | Signed | Sci        | Short    | Count | Hex | Bits |
| ------ | --------- | ------ | ---------- | -------- | ----- | --- | ---- |
| Tea    | 12345.678 | 2.25   | 123456.789 | 0.000012 | 42    | 255 | 5    |
| Coffee | 3.5       | -0.04  | 0.5        | 1e21     | -7    | -1  | 255  |
| Cake   | 19.995    | 0      | 1e-10      | 100      | 0     | 0   | 0    |
